<title>USA: U.S. to give $15 million more in N. Korea aid.</title>
<headline>U.S. to give $15 million more in N. Korea aid.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States on Tuesday announced $15 million in additional food aid to feed children in famine-threatened North Korea.</p>
<p>State Department spokesman Nicholas Burns said the new U.S. donation, taking total U.S. food aid to Pyongyang to $33.4 million, was decided upon because North Korea's food shortages would reach a critical stage this spring.</p>
</text>
